    isbefore: []  # d917
    duplicate_of: []  # d917
    not_duplicate_of: []  # d917
    pr_ref:  # d917
    description: "**Wave-2 identity gate finding (2026-06-16), CLASS 2 — adversarially verified, skeptic could NOT refute (high confidence).**\n\n**Mechanic.** The http and database-query linkers mint `call_site` stand-in Symbols whose `stable_id` is keyed on endpoint/query CONTENT with NO file path and NO occurrence index:\n- `linkers/http.py:1338` — `_create_client_symbol()` sets `stable_id=make_route_stable_id(call.method, _extract_path_from_url(call.url) or call.url)`; `make_route_stable_id` (analyze/base.py:523-548) hashes only `route:{method}:{normalized_path}`. `_extract_path_from_url` strips host+query, so \"GET http://localhost/api/users\" and \"GET /api/users\" in different files hash identically.\n- `linkers/database_query.py:373` — `_create_query_symbol()` sets `stable_id=make_protocol_stable_id(\"db_query\", query_type, sorted-tables)`; `make_protocol_stable_id` (base.py:744-748) hashes only `db_query:{type}:{tables}`. `rel_path` is computed at database_query.py:346 and discarded from the hash.\n\n**Why it's a real violation (not by-design).** ADR-0035 §3's kind→axis table ALREADY classifies `call_site (http)` (producer http.py:1326) and `call_site (sql)` (producer database_query.py:355) as **SITE**, key `(path, target, occurrence idx)` — so these producers violate their OWN declared axis by omitting `path`. The shared `stable_id` is NOT load-bearing: both linkers build their `calls`/`references` edges on `Symbol.id` (path+line, genuinely per-file unique), and client↔server matching is by URL-pattern match, not stable_id equality. The client `call_site` is the CALLER's location (SITE); the route handler is the LOGICAL endpoint hub. Collapsing two callers to one stable_id is exactly the per-call-metadata loss the graphql LOGICAL-exclusion comment (base.py:949-956) warns against.\n\n**Scope.** 31 cross-file colliding nodes across SELF, caddy, httpx, koel (http) and SELF, sqlalchemy (sql) in the Wave-2 gate cohort. Within-file is already clean (split_within_file_stable_id_collisions handles `(path, stable_id)` groups; cross-file is untouched by construction).\n\n**Fix (factory + post-pass + content-gated validator).** Fold the repo-relative file path into the producer hash so the §3 SITE key `(path, target, occurrence idx)` is honored at mint (path-anchored site factory, e.g. `make_site_stable_id(protocol_origin, rel_path, target)`, threading rel_path already in scope at both producers). Keep `split_within_file_stable_id_collisions` for the within-file occurrence index. Add a kind→axis-aware corpus validator asserting SITE-axis kinds whose hash omits `path` are an error (the ADR-0035 §5 \"kind→axis conformance\" limb currently only verifies kind-in-registry, not LOGICAL/SITE hash SHAPE). Do NOT add http/db_query to `_LOGICAL_DEDUP_PROTOCOL_ORIGINS` (that manufactures by-design collisions — the graphql lesson). This is a hash-input change → rides a coordinated scheme bump (ADR-0035 §6 atomicity), bundled with the route decision (see sibling decision item) into one v7→v8 train.\n\nNote: the existing test `test_http_linker.py::test_same_url_produces_same_stable_id` asserts the colliding behavior — it is pre-ADR-0035 unmigrated residue (§5 \"producer fix deferred\"), and must be updated when this fix lands. Evidence: ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/wave2_identity_gate_06162026_1904.md."  # d917
    fields: {}  # d917
